  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kumkale TKY</p>\r\n<p>Cook 1973 87 argues for the placement of a Roman harbor town by the name of Aianteion, although argues against a Greek precursor in the same location as the territory would have, at the point, belonged to Rhoeteum.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Aianteion was a port town in the Troad located near the putative Tomb of Ajax, with which it shared a name.",
